<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 11 November, from 1215 to 1965.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">Remembrance Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed each year at the eleventh hour of the eleventh day of the eleventh month — the moment the Armistice ending the First World War took effect in 1918 — Remembrance Day honours the sacrifice of military personnel who have died in all wars since.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1215 <span class="tih-ago">811 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent III opens the Fourth Lateran Council</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The largest church council of the Middle Ages met in Rome under Innocent III. It defined transubstantiation, required annual confession and ordered Jews and Muslims to wear distinguishing dress.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/virginia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virginia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1831 <span class="tih-ago">195 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nat Turner is hanged in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nat Turner was executed at Jerusalem, Virginia, for leading the August revolt in which about 55 to 60 white people were killed. Reprisals killed many more Black people, and southern states tightened slave codes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The armistice ends fighting on the Western Front</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed at 5 a.m. in a railway carriage in the forest of Compiègne, the armistice between Germany and the Allies took effect at 11 o'clock. The day is marked as Armistice or Remembrance Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1921 <span class="tih-ago">105 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier is dedicated at Arlington</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Harding presided as an unidentified American soldier from the Western Front was buried at Arlington National Cemetery. A year earlier, Britain and France had interred their own unknown warriors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zimbabwe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rhodesia declares independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ian Smith's white minority government issued a Unilateral Declaration of Independence to avoid majority rule. Britain and the UN imposed sanctions, and after a long guerrilla war Zimbabwe became independent in 1980.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a></div></div></li></ol>
